WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.434
-Yeah, it is good to be here,
but thank you for --

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.901
-You seem like
you're in a bad mood.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.601
-I am in a bad mood.
Sorry. I am in a bad mood.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:07.734
-Why?

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:10.534
-Because you bring
me out after Taylor Swift

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.100
and, like, all of
the excitement, the biggest --

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.601
one of the biggest stars,

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.167
and then it's deliberately
to sabotage

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.434
that I come out here.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.801
-I'm not doing this
to sabotage you. I would --

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:22.701
-I come out here
in a corduroy shirt.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:25.033
-I could hear you walking out
before you even came.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.434
I'm actually so happy
that you're here

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.334
and I want to talk to you about
"The Last Best Hope,"

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.033
but I want to talk about,
just in general,

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:35.701
I saw somewhere that --

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.434
You're in such a bad mood.

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.701
Such a punk.
You are such a punk, man.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:44.000
-You were holding it
sarcastically.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.367
-I wasn't holding
it sarcastically.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.868
-I'll hold it.
-I was holding in reverence.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.834
-I'll hold it.
-Oh, gosh. Alright.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.200
I wanted to ask you a thing,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.000
because I think this is
a compliment for you.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.167
A lot of teachers --
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.234
-They're are asking you
for your last special

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.934
to be put online, because they
want to teach it to their --

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.334
They're teaching it
to their students.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.634
-Actually,
they're not asking me.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.968
They just use it.
Nobody's paying for it.

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.701
No money, no credit,
just use it at their classes.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:15.667
But I am grateful for it.
I know it sounds like I'm not.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:19.868
Because I consider myself --

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.367
I was always in that role with
Jimmy at "SNL."

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.334
I was really
a mentor and a teacher to you.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:29.434
You were just a young,
wet-behind-the-ears boy,

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:33.534
and I told you -- I'm the reason
you have this show.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:34.667
Remember what I said
when you were there?

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.868
-What is going --

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.667
-And I remember telling you --
Early on, I said,

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.634
"When you leave the show, do
a couple of unwatchable movies.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:44.133
Then go into talk-show...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.801
What did I say?
-This is unbelievable.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.300
-Hey, come on. Oh!

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.367
-Which one?

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.400
Give me that...

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.467
Which one was unwatchable?
-Oh...

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:55.000
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.200
-But this is -- Look at this.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.534
You're doing material that is

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.734
going to go in
the educational system.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.267
-I know. It is good.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.300
-What kind of changes would you
make if you were a teacher?

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.400
What would you say
to these kids?

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.634
What do they have to learn?

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.701
-Well, here's the problem,
is our education system,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.000
we teach what?

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.033
Study hard, bear down,
you'll be a success in life.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.667
-Yeah.
-That's not our system.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:16.834
We're a sales country.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.901
We should be teaching kids
that the person

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.634
that studies hard, that goes to
work and just works,

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.067
and doesn't talk to anybody,
they go,

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.467
"That's the office psycho."

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:27.367
We're -- Teach personality.

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.601
Kids should be taught
first day of preschool --

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.167
Everyone has social anxiety.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.667
Teach your kids to walk in
and memorize --

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.934
Like, just walk in first day of
preschool and be like,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.067
"Is it me or is this
bus driver a little off?"

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.534
Something like that.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:44.167
You know, get people to...

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.601
-A little bit off.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.133
-Teach them how
to work the crowd.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.834
That's who does well
in our country,

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.000
the people that walk in
and be like,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.400
"See? This kid knows what
I'm talking about."

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.734
The kid doesn't even know.
They're like this.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.200
But you're like, "You get it.
You get it."

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.667
Just bond.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.067
You're like, "The other kids --
I don't know if they get it.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.367
You know, they're like zombies.
You get it, you know?

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.801
We need more kids like you in
this class, I'll be honest.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.934
Not a lot of us left."

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.767
It's a personality country.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:07.868
-Yeah, it is.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.100
-I just want...

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.501
Hold up.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.701
Yo! Sit down!

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.834
-You're holding it
sarcastically.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.767
You're holding it sarcastically.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.200
Chris, Chris, how can I --

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.634
Chris, how can I help you?

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:33.033
-I just came to
see Taylor Swift, Jimmy.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.534
-No, you missed Taylor Swift.

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:37.934
-Are these all military people?
-Yes, these are all military.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes!

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.000
25% got fake vaccines.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.133
-Chris, good to see you,
as always.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.501
You missed Taylor.
I'll send you a link.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:49.968
-Alright.
-I'll send you a link.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.133
Chris Rock, everybody.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.667
-Oh, that's great, Jimmy. Nice.
That was accidental, too?

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:06.067
Hey, let's bring out

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:09.133
Harry Styles
and Olivia Wilde next.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.767
-Colin, when I talk about
"The Last Best Hope,"

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.000
you're going to go on
the road with this.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.434
You're going to travel
the country.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.701
-Oh, sure I am.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.901
But this is -- Can I ask you
about this, though?

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:23.400
"The Last Best Hope" --
who is the the last best hope?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.701
-Well, it's a quote from Lincoln

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.434
about the country
being the last best hope.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.534
But in this case,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.000
it's "Colin Quinn,
The Last Best Hope."

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.501
I mean...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.501
-"Colin Quinn,
The Last Best Hope"

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.501
is running now
through November 20th

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.100
here in New York,
then heading to

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.334
cities across the U.S.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.634
For tickets,
go to colinquinn.com.

